{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00145",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.32,
      "end_seconds": 4.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Oh, hello, doctor. Where would you like me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.48,
      "end_seconds": 8.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.08,
      "end_seconds": 18.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.34,
      "text": "So, So the thing is, I've got a fever for days. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.88,
      "end_seconds": 20.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.2,
      "end_seconds": 28.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "For about four days, I'd say. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.73,
      "end_seconds": 38.86,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.93,
      "end_seconds": 58.53,
      "duration_seconds": 18.6,
      "text": "I get some relief from paracetamol. It's a few times a day. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I've had constipation too, for about two weeks. There's a bad headache as well. About bad headache, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.04,
      "end_seconds": 66.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Right, have you had a fever for days before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.06,
      "end_seconds": 75.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "I, I had a similar thing last winter. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.41,
      "end_seconds": 78.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Have you had any cough or jaundice?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.76,
      "end_seconds": 81.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.27,
      "end_seconds": 87.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any vomiting, burning when passing urine or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.25,
      "end_seconds": 92.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.76,
      "end_seconds": 96.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.91,
      "end_seconds": 99.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.27,
      "end_seconds": 101.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.77,
      "end_seconds": 105.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.03,
      "end_seconds": 108.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.53,
      "end_seconds": 112.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.28,
      "end_seconds": 117.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.03,
      "end_seconds": 124.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "I have diabetes. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.96,
      "end_seconds": 133.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "Alright. Right, so that's your known diabetes. We'll keep that in mind today. Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.48,
      "end_seconds": 137.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.74,
      "end_seconds": 142.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.96,
      "end_seconds": 143.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.91,
      "end_seconds": 150.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.09,
      "end_seconds": 153.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I'm on glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.27,
      "end_seconds": 157.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.13,
      "end_seconds": 160.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "About two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.09,
      "end_seconds": 163.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.05,
      "end_seconds": 170.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.09,
      "end_seconds": 199.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 96 percent, pulse is 89 beats a minute. And blood pressure 121 over 77, temperature is 38.2 degrees, respiratory rate 21."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.06,
      "end_seconds": 202.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.96,
      "end_seconds": 205.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.06,
      "end_seconds": 212.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.28,
      "end_seconds": 215.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.87,
      "end_seconds": 227.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Your tummy is a bit full and tender in the lower part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.27,
      "end_seconds": 231.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.36,
      "end_seconds": 252.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "I can't feel your liver or spleen enlarged."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.99,
      "end_seconds": 282.66,
      "duration_seconds": 24.67,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.22,
      "end_seconds": 286.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.1,
      "end_seconds": 297.2,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is typhoid fever, which we need to confirm. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.75,
      "end_seconds": 302.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Well, um, should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.01,
      "end_seconds": 321.81,
      "duration_seconds": 18.8,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's typhoid fever, which we need to confirm, and we'll know more once the a malaria test is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a fever for days for about four days, and no vomiting or cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.12,
      "end_seconds": 323.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.87,
      "end_seconds": 347.21,
      "duration_seconds": 22.34,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a malaria test for fever. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'm prescribing paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. You take it by mouth. That's for fever and body aches. Eat only home-cooked food and drink boiled or bottled water while this is going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.46,
      "end_seconds": 367.36,
      "duration_seconds": 18.9,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. If the fever stays high or the tummy pain gets sharp, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Let's review you in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.28,
      "end_seconds": 372.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Um, uh, okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.71,
      "end_seconds": 380.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.54,
      "end_seconds": 390.32,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "So, I take the paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed and come back in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.68,
      "end_seconds": 396.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.99,
      "end_seconds": 399.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, doctor, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.51,
      "end_seconds": 402.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}